# The toolchain writes LF: the generator, tsc, and the GitHub Actions runners that commit
# data/ and output/ on a schedule. Every blob in this repo is already LF. Without this rule,
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows checks files out as CRLF, and any file the generator then
# rewrites is stuck reporting "modified" with an empty git diff — permanently, since
# `git update-index --refresh` cannot clear it. Pinning eol=lf makes checkout agree with
# what the tools write, so `git status` means what it says again.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Photos and brand marks. Auto-detection would catch these, but declaring them costs nothing
# and keeps the intent readable beside the xlsx rule below.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary

# Generated workbooks are zip archives. Git's binary auto-detection would almost certainly
# catch them, but "almost" is the wrong bet for a committed artifact — a CRLF conversion
# inside a deflate stream produces a file Excel refuses to open.
*.xlsx binary
